#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096444 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "e47a8da7-9276-5f4c-8ee6-1fd737c2e9ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-4277" :question/problem "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](images/04/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/53/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/81/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/id #uuid "0b0dbbc1-d39d-5aff-9f16-075779d36659" :question/math-academy-id "e-5015" :question/problem "![](images/24/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nI. $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\nII. $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\nIII. $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "c7526e18-37a9-572a-a6a3-0384bbccf41d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9934" :question/problem "![](images/74/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/49/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/08/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367788ba-9c7c-5e7c-8d21-94b3c4ba0009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244796} {:answer/id #uuid "8f148817-c745-530a-a8b8-28d7b5e4345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=c-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245562} {:answer/id #uuid "b417d004-817e-5033-a8fd-22b425d08539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a-b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245918} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e4a15b-18c4-5947-9ba2-a025c8d4e9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a+b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245957} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bce547-b8ee-520e-ad41-e9f53f4bdc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d+a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367788ba-9c7c-5e7c-8d21-94b3c4ba0009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244796} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcf588e-a428-59ae-a4f9-9b453b8f13ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4193f1f9-5dd6-5e42-ab53-c9d471fede26" :question/math-academy-id "q-11323" :question/problem "![](images/36/36aaf58af536428c74cdb8f4c02c2b4f07e414422e8aea378c75d7abcff58cff.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{YX}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{XV}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{VZ}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{XW}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $X$ to $W$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$  \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XW}=\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW},\n$$\n\nas shown below. \n\n![](images/47/4758b51fd3dc076059d60e944de0ad8375bb304240365959d4c6cae94f95a535.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XY}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/e9/e942d61c1f51c36dc6cd04f88ff5e37f538920a34c1af5bc780c47691567b668.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XW} & =\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW} \\\\  & =-a+d \\\\  & =d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c4d8ad-5f55-5ce6-83f3-6a8835fd2263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=-c+a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523400} {:answer/id #uuid "785556b5-a9bc-5d2d-aa4a-8e78cf699f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=c+a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523499} {:answer/id #uuid "87397bfe-0e30-5921-8557-cb215a45b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=c-a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523538} {:answer/id #uuid "945d9463-cce8-5a6e-94de-eeeeb592a448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=c+a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523566} {:answer/id #uuid "a5798b1a-1da6-5a8e-82f0-4ba4c3d308de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=-c+a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87397bfe-0e30-5921-8557-cb215a45b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=c-a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a34cbc2-3857-5f7b-a15a-6c328746d865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eceb91e0-95b6-5672-af4d-3210bb9c13a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12046" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b441f7b59f59240141380711d5d380ea58cafa01f8a288f1e5c8bc7685650cf.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,$ and $c.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f7/f728becaa8903fc0aa17ea9d15dd7199447dd70eff5b4a3d2be5982f1eeca8a5.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{SP}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/05/055bb2c63c42defaa9f624f20b8ad92dd80f3d34b0d689def859b34785318749.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =-b+(-a)+c \\\\  & =c-a-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60fa9802-8c91-55e9-84a5-e1363e2e7308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387010} {:answer/id #uuid "9d30e4cd-7866-5dc8-9d17-e3603b0e1d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387011} {:answer/id #uuid "0e6b1f27-9577-571f-a402-5318532c66a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387012} {:answer/id #uuid "6efc2e18-f131-54ef-8b65-97d65d26fb87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387013} {:answer/id #uuid "4939a251-4f3d-5483-a371-05ba68aaf27c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e6b1f27-9577-571f-a402-5318532c66a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387012} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e3c074-2fe2-56ad-8be9-99fa6a58e9b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b958283a-525c-51ab-a33e-68049ee3df0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-12049" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f9e6eff196e24ddabca8d778d27e499fc1b856ef7169257a31a7cbaca8b564b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e1d5eb2f392332f69fa1507899b30b838a42ebd1c40dacddeca4edcf0f7aa8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=-b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/0e/0e8e24968141284550fac7d4e5c63333789f30ade8f7d5dd8b87fae4e012673a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =a+(-b) \\\\  & =a-b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090bb1db-63a6-54df-9f65-16399002d7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523274} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd743ae-6000-5ea5-bd2f-d16d353506d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523348} {:answer/id #uuid "45c1bb40-2367-52da-b024-e48e8c24cd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523397} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8f1b84-13b6-5114-bb9e-ab24fa1f8c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523412} {:answer/id #uuid "e777df4b-9aba-50b2-9b75-be3f2a7d5536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c8f1b84-13b6-5114-bb9e-ab24fa1f8c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523412} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea2b4e97-a8a3-5689-bdb9-c780153e0b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ccb8873-58fb-5db3-858e-4560c5c188b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-143003" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3abecc8d3b60b6c9796fc9c9449888c700d205aad90786fa9e4fee854cdc07e1.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{BO}?$\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AD}-\\overset{\\to }{OD}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" :question/worked-solution "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AD}-\\overset{\\to }{OD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AD})+\\overset{\\to }{DO} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DO} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BO}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{CO} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BO}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BO}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f09596-2658-5073-a3eb-3e27627b85c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523335} {:answer/id #uuid "a2189126-0c2c-57d3-b1ab-1faf368a33ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523592} {:answer/id #uuid "b34ec392-fde6-5d28-8102-c76e7c6273f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523633} {:answer/id #uuid "be872f56-07d9-5cdd-93a0-3ef13124098b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523652} {:answer/id #uuid "c288c24a-395b-59d2-8695-f05a71c1d9fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be872f56-07d9-5cdd-93a0-3ef13124098b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523652} :answer-field/id #uuid "e045fd4c-49c5-5aab-8afb-9ed4d45a7fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a225df54-1e5c-59a8-9085-a55a59c0af5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143004" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0009b057eef7d5d4e380883f26442b2c4e5777e90c77a7fd7791506c87cbcd4.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDE$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{BE}?$\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{DE}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}$" :question/worked-solution "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA})+\\overset{\\to }{AE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD})+\\overset{\\to }{DE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "356e33e8-c745-5aad-839c-9497e2a771c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "356e33e8-c745-5aad-839c-9497e2a771c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523365} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b88b3c0-25b5-5b3c-b29d-2c7183c7d6ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae6e233b-a8cc-54d7-a535-be00579ec6e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-328092" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c895d3f634102ff747342616f572b6a2fa8a57c86215f20b47d2187e6e7f96d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{DA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{AB}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{BC}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DE}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{DC}$ in terms of vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{DC}=$  \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $D$ to $C$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd94c2f43b5da5252879f8acdcc14fc2f951f9a899903482bd3947ca8ec6921e.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{DA}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{BC}=c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/e0/e0f53eb04be491e8b84e2c7d5d252ab2c04bdfe372a93a503788a1ee94f63675.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & =a+b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543fc7ef-7426-502e-9e08-f734a83baccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "543fc7ef-7426-502e-9e08-f734a83baccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523423} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f6fb77a-3236-5ed3-8a05-0105cce190eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95308c1b-5af9-5c02-9df1-10249ec99ede" :question/math-academy-id "q-332559" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b65d3044591af808c6f27f54e7bfb723b053b66c335929e96c18624c94233b3.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{BA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{FA}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{FE}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{CE}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{CB}$ in terms of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{CB}=$   \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $C$ to $B$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}+\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/18/18b8d39937dd23f03a030727e642729259ec5ab0c6fcb438c8bf82a2b7aaf08d.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CE}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EF}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{FA}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/6f/6f1c084747ad1b0de2ab28979fee8e14db9463f1d82d07ab787581789bcb6e37.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}+\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =d-c+b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "646276d7-3118-5a12-8f30-753005b5d0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646276d7-3118-5a12-8f30-753005b5d0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523459} :answer-field/id #uuid "86338cc0-f301-5ecc-b080-e1a93da8083a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eccc4fe9-82af-5d0c-a3d1-d04e0240d4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-335834" :question/problem "![](images/83/837da5064b1f09449bf10caa6738dbe276d71e922a5a4fa96566010fb8ae320a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{AE}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{DB}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{CB}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{EC}$ in terms of  $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{EC}=$   \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $E$ to $C$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{EC}=\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/a8/a8b76bf9fc26742d8ba05c962e59986e9f7b596f0b02c8e71c4ead4b45cf542a.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{EA}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{AD}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{DB}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{BC}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/fe/fe663b4bfacc4ef2078e014af664e99123cb803fd26d03a449bf9bf6198629cc.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{EC} & =\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & =-a+d+b+(-c) \\\\  & =-a+d+b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0286ec20-cb3e-596c-b47d-f7e1f3c57be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=c-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523257} {:answer/id #uuid "04f65fe2-47e2-5951-8c41-5a049b5e1467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523261} {:answer/id #uuid "37cafaee-d6a9-58e0-a53c-93c9c0fc2d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=b-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523372} {:answer/id #uuid "585ac67c-f323-55e2-a9f2-ac9a32e